.cache/
__pycache__/
keys.json

# Yours, not the app's. marks.json holds saved views by name, which for a
# real user means the coordinates of real homes; targets.json holds the places
# you are watching for movement, which is the same kind of list; usage.json is
# a running tally of what you have spent at Google. Examples ship instead.
data/marks.json
data/targets.json
data/usage.json
data/manual_events.json

# What the hidden server said. It runs with no window now, so its output goes
# here instead of to a console nobody is watching - and the launcher reads these
# back to you if it fails to come up.
server.log
server-error.log

# A Windows shortcut stores an absolute path, so the one that works here is
# broken everywhere else. The .cmd files beside it work from any folder.
*.lnk

# Written when the launcher has asked Windows to fetch the certificate
# authorities the app needs. Local to the machine it ran on.
.certificates-warmed

# Local workstation backup notes; not part of published releases.
BEFORE-IMPROVEMENTS.md
